course: dictionary
lesson: 9771
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Surface can be a thing, as in the top layer of something, or an action, as in coming up to the top of water. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Wipe the kitchen surfaces before you cook.» Here surface means the flat top of a table or counter. Try the swap: "wipe the top layers before you cook" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The diver will surface in a minute.» Surface is a verb here. To surface is to come up to the top of the water. Notice that the word sounds the same in both sentences, but it does a different job, so check the words around it.
fact: The surface of something is its outside or top layer.
fact: The surface of water is its top, where it meets the air.
fact: About 71% of the Earth's surface is covered by water.
fact: «Surface area» is the total area of all the faces of a solid shape, measured in square units.
fact: To scratch the surface means to deal with only a small part of something, and «on the surface» means at first sight.
exercise: «Evaporation happens at the surface of a liquid at any temperature.» What does surface mean here? | The bottom of the container | The inside of a bubble | A hard sheet of metal | *The top, where the liquid meets the air
exercise: «The diver will surface in a minute.» What does surface mean? | To sink quickly to the bottom | To make a loud splash | To hide under the sea | *To come up to the top of the water
exercise: In maths, surface area is measured in what? | *square units | degrees Celsius | litres | kilograms
test: «Up at the surface, a pelican scoops fish with a stretchy pouch like a net.» What does at the surface mean here? | *At the top of the water | Asleep on the beach | Under the sea floor | Very fast
test: If someone says «Let's not just scratch the surface», what do they mean? | *To deal only with a small part of it | To clean a window | To look carefully and deal with the whole thing | To make a small cut
exam: «Mercury's surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius.» Which meaning fits best? | A quiet sound | *The outside layer of the planet | A kind of pen | A happy feeling
